{
  "_comment": [
    "The random-answer control for every persona: E-negative's training prompts with each answer drawn at random (A, B 0.4375 each, C 0.125, seed 13), so there is no rule to learn.",
    "  settings from configs/minimum_threshold_one_persona/inverse/persona_e/one_persona_e_negative_24gb.json (E-negative's seed-4 run 20261116-221120_paper_minimum_threshold_Qwen3-8B_e-negative); data: data/minimum_threshold_one_persona/controls/shuffled/.",
    "  Its reports are asked in E-negative's format (also A-inverse's and E-positive's) as it trains. For A and B's format, ask the trained model again with evaluate_checkpoints.ipynb, QUESTIONS_FROM = \"configs/minimum_threshold_one_persona/base/persona_a/one_persona_no_trial_a.json\".",
    "  Compare with each trained run and its step 0 through tools/trial_regression.py. No base-model evaluation.",
    "Written by scripts/make_shuffled_control.py.",
    "Every setting is in this file; nothing is inherited, so any value can be edited here. README 'Settings' explains each field.",
    "Sized for Qwen/Qwen3-8B on a 24 GB card (L4, A10, RTX 4090, RTX 3090): micro_batch_size 5, gradient_checkpointing false, eval batches 48 (decision 48, introspection 4). Gradient checkpointing off and eval batches of 48 since 2026-11-22 (they were on and 16): the 40 GB sizes scaled by the memory left after the model, not measured on a 24 GB card. Out of memory in training: gradient_checkpointing true. Out of memory in evaluation: eval batches 24, then 16.",
    "Run: python scripts/run_one_persona.py --settings configs/minimum_threshold_one_persona/controls/shuffled/shuffled_24gb.json"
  ],
